{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Like the stranger, like the citizen.</b> And it does not say 'the stranger like the citizen,' for then it would be understood that the status of the stranger is below the status of the citizen, since the lesser is hitched to the greater. Therefore it says <b>like the stranger, like the citizen</b> — meaning, the citizen is like the stranger and the stranger is like the citizen, for they are equal in judgment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:39.165285195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}